  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed specifically for death in military combat. Not used for civilian casualties or deaths in peacetime. The suru verb form {戦死|せんし}する means \"to be killed in battle.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {戦死|せんし}する: to die in battle\n- {戦死|せんし}した{兵士|へいし}: soldiers killed in action\n- {戦死|せんし}{者|しゃ}: war dead, those killed in battle\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {戦没|せんぼつ}: death in war (more formal, often used in memorial contexts)\n- {殉職|じゅんしょく}: death in the line of duty (not limited to military)",
